6-03-24T18:58:23Z", "updated_at": "2026-07-06T06:31:46Z", "closed_at": "2026-07-06T06:31:46Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "`promtool` allows pushing arbitrary metric files to a Prometheus compatible remote write endpoint. But only if the endpoint path ends with `/api/v1/write`.\n\nThe problem being that `/api/v1/write` is always appended to the url given to promtool.\n`http://localhost:8080/my/ep -> http://localhost:8080/my/ep/api/v1/write`\n\nMimir specifically only accepts metrics on `/api/v1/push` and promtool currently does not allow any way to overwrite this aside from prefixing the default path.\n\nThe Path is always appended with the default path value \"/api/v1/write\".\nhttps://github.com/prometheus/client_golang/blob/8f78afd82a7fa242c008ec04280a9a836ee28808/exp/api/remote/remote_api.go#L151\n\nhttps://github.com/prometheus/client_golang/blob/8f78afd82a7fa242c008ec04280a9a836ee28808/exp/api/remote/remote_api.go#L81\n\nBut the API options include the `WithAPIPath` func which allows overwriting the default:\nhttps://github.com/prometheus/client_golang/blob/8f78afd82a7fa242c008ec04280a9a836ee28808/exp/api/remote/remote_api.go#L101-L107\n\nWould you consider either changing the behaviour of how the `<url>` path is handled to instead overwrite the default path or alternatively be open to a PR adding a new parameter allowing users to override the default path?", "closed_by": {"login": "dgl", "id": 5385, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjUzODU=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5385?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/dgl", "html_url": "https://github.com/dgl", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/dgl/followers", "following_url": "http